parseWorkbench: validate title, tool identities, labels, supported actions and typed references; return definition.
workbenchReferences: validate JSON and create a retained Array of target and argument objects.
workbench: ensure a rooted ordinary Workbench and read its current definition.
handleWorkbench: expose the live workbench identity and definition through GET.
readExample: read editable text and scratch workspace identity from a live example.
listExamples: traverse the workbench's owned example Array in order and describe each entry.
handleExamples: expose catalog data through GET.

Accept services and session as declarative tool actions.
